Original commit body from d7f957336682e964090aa51812fc8ae0bc8a0333:

verify_taint_claim hardcoded the literal string "approximate" into every
violated verdict's details, and _flow_evidence_dict dropped confidence and
analysis_method entirely. So the ADR-0017 section 3a walk could confirm a flow
by data dependence and BOTH surfaces a user reads would still say the analysis
was approximate. The label was produced and then discarded -- the same
provenance discontinuity section 3a itself was built to close, one layer down.

Two consequences worth stating. No consumer could have noticed the hardcoded
literal, because the field it contradicted was not emitted either. And the two
preceding commits' improvements were, until now, invisible from every CLI
surface -- they had to be measured with an instrument wrapping the propagator.

Each evidence row carries confidence + analysis_method; each verdict carries an
analysis_methods breakdown. The breakdown mirrors flow_origins (WI-vazal): the
structured field is the contract, the prose a courtesy. analysis_method is the
finer axis and the one worth carrying -- confidence collapses ddg_mixed (the
walk ran and did not confirm) and structural (no reaching-def data existed, so
no walk was possible) into one approximate bucket, and "the analysis looked and
found nothing" is a different fact about a security verdict from "the analysis
could not look".

THE AGGREGATION POLICY IS STATED, NOT LEFT TO max(). A verdict is a DISJUNCTION
over its flows and after section 3a those flows can be adjudicated differently.
Collapsing upward would claim a precision most flows did not have; collapsing
downward would erase the ones that earned it. So the composition is reported --
[host_secret confidence: 9 approximate, 1 precise] -- with the single-value case
staying terse, which keeps the rendering byte-identical for a verdict whose
flows all agree. That uniformity is precisely why the literal went unnoticed.

Both breakdowns count every counted flow, not the shown rows: evidence is
deduplicated and capped, details counts every violation, and a breakdown over
the shown rows would silently disagree with the total printed beside it.

to_dict dropped the new field on the first pass and a red test caught it. Same
defect class in miniature -- a dataclass field the serializer omits is
discarded as completely as one never computed, and is HARDER to notice because
every in-process test still sees it.

MEASURED, 9-repo cohort against the pre-change baseline: ZERO verdicts move.
54 verdict rows, 0 changed on (verdict, evidence_count, shown rows); 38
confirmed / 16 violated both arms. That null is the point of the check (L57 --
when the correct result is "no change", a broken build looks identical to a
correct one), so it is paired with a positive control: 16 verdicts now carry a
populated analysis_methods, cohort-wide {ddg_mixed: 300, ddg: 8, structural: 3}.
Live repro on caddy through the real CLI: analysis_methods {'ddg': 1,
'ddg_mixed': 9} with the matching evidence row labelled confidence=precise /
analysis_method=ddg.

Two stale prose claims corrected in place. TaintFlowFinding.analysis_method's
inline comment read "structural" or "ddg" while the propagator had been
assigning ddg_mixed, so a reader enumerating the vocabulary from the field
declaration got it wrong. The module docstring's "structural analysis produces
approximate confidence" was equally incomplete once section 3a shipped.

Envelope schema 1.3 -> 1.4, additive.

